    "description": "Siege workshop, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Over budget: 487 blocks vs 300 (first build 423). Open-sided timber shed where engineers build siege engines: a catapult in the yard before the open front (L2 adds its arm and cup), crafting table, log piles, a catslide tool store; L3 a long battering ram in its frame, lanterns.",
    "changes": "Quality-check notes: the shed moved 3 rows back so the catapult stands out in a cobble yard in front of the open gable, its tail under the roof: dark rails, wheels, a braced A-frame with its stop bar and the axle already at L1, the throwing arm and cup over the bar at L2. The front tie beam is raised to y 5 with braces, the front gable closed above it (plaster, king post); the back gable has no hole (stone wall with a shuttered window, plaster gable with a king post). The sawhorse slabs sit on fence legs (no floating slabs). The tool store is a sloped catslide lean-to with stone walls (west). Less brown: stone plinths under the posts, stone walls, a cobble yard, bushes and poppies on the grass. L3: a long ram (8 dark oak logs and a capped head) hanging on chains from two trestles on the east side, plus lanterns, a pile of stone shot and more flowers.",
